{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270548",
      "title": "Understanding the useCallback() Hook",
      "sourceHash": "7bf5b30d65535936c38814c88007f034400133b5f5356ad60af6d2e5ce5f51f6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "Now even though memo couldn't to be honest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 7.65,
          "en": "should be removed here, I wanna take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.65,
          "end": 11.04,
          "en": "at using memo, and I'll use it on another component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.04,
          "end": 13.893,
          "en": "a component down here in the counter component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.12,
          "end": 17.79,
          "en": "Because of course at the moment in this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.79,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "if I increment the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 21.3,
          "en": "we get a bunch of component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.3,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "being re executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 25.98,
          "en": "To be precise we got these icon buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.98,
          "end": 27.42,
          "en": "and icons executing again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.42,
          "end": 29.223,
          "en": "and of course the counter output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.54,
          "end": 32.88,
          "en": "Now the counter output makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.88,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "because of course that output does change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 36.42,
          "en": "whenever I click a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.42,
          "end": 39.063,
          "en": "So this of course needs to be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 42.6,
          "en": "But for these buttons it's different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "Of course, those button components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 47.31,
          "en": "and the values they output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.31,
          "end": 49.47,
          "en": "of course technically don't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 50.91,
          "en": "It's always exactly this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 50.91,
          "end": 54.333,
          "en": "and this button that gets output when I press a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.2,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "So re-rendering these components, re-executing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "these component functions doesn't make a lot of sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "Now, as mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 66.9,
          "en": "it also isn't a huge problem in this app though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.9,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "because these components contain so little code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "that executing them is no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 76.89,
          "en": "But still, we could wrap icon button with memo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.89,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "to make sure it's not getting re‐executed unnecessarily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "And since it's in this icon button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 85.95,
          "en": "where the actual icon is being rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.95,
          "end": 90.06,
          "en": "the icon component therefore also won't be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.06,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "So we'll prevent the execution of two components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "by just wrapping one of them with memo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 99.39,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, we can import memo here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.39,
          "end": 102.90299999999999,
          "en": "from React in the icon button component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.00999999999999,
          "end": 107.28,
          "en": "And then just as before, create a new constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.28,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "and wrap this component function with memo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 115.833,
          "en": "and then export this newly created constant like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "If we do that, you'll notice something strange though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 126,
          "en": "If you reload, clear this and click this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126,
          "end": 129.42,
          "en": "Hmm, it still got executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.42,
          "end": 132.46,
          "en": "So looks like memo didn't work here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.47,
          "end": 137.34,
          "en": "or it did work and some prop value changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.34,
          "end": 138.69,
          "en": "But for that, let's take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.69,
          "end": 141.393,
          "en": "at the props accepted by icon button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.89,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "It's the children prop, which is output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.57999999999998,
          "end": 149.94,
          "en": "and that in the end is simply the text of the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.94,
          "end": 153,
          "en": "So the button is wrapped around this text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "and that's therefore the value that's fed in as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 157.203,
          "en": "for children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.34,
          "end": 161.91,
          "en": "Now obviously those texts here don't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.91,
          "end": 165.423,
          "en": "So the prop value for children shouldn't have changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.1,
          "end": 168.63,
          "en": "Now what about icon?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.63,
          "end": 173.63,
          "en": "The icon prop in the end receives a pointer to a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.79,
          "end": 178.23,
          "en": "the name of a component, but not the component as JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.23,
          "end": 181.8,
          "en": "That's important just the name of the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.8,
          "end": 186.21,
          "en": "and it then translates it to JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.21,
          "end": 189.033,
          "en": "inside of this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.71,
          "end": 193.47,
          "en": "But clearly these pointers here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.47,
          "end": 197.25,
          "en": "these names of these components are also not dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 199.53,
          "en": "and also shouldn't change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.53,
          "end": 202.683,
          "en": "when the counter component function is being executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.66,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "So it must be related to the remaining props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 210.22,
          "en": "which we got here, which I'm just forwarding to the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.32,
          "end": 213.84,
          "en": "And here I am just setting one other prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.84,
          "end": 216.753,
          "en": "and that's onClick, which I set to a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.04,
          "end": 220.47,
          "en": "And this indeed is the problem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.47,
          "end": 225.47,
          "en": "because these functions look as if they maybe don't change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.63,
          "end": 229.17000000000002,
          "en": "but keep in mind that they are created inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.17000000000002,
          "end": 231.15,
          "en": "of the counter component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.15,
          "end": 235.56,
          "en": "These are nested functions, and therefore, indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.56,
          "end": 239.099,
          "en": "they will technically be recreated every time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.099,
          "end": 242.58,
          "en": "this counter component function executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.58,
          "end": 247.56,
          "en": "So every time this state changes, and it does not matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.56,
          "end": 249.87,
          "en": "that the code in there is the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.87,
          "end": 254.22,
          "en": "and does not change, the component function as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.22,
          "end": 258.33,
          "en": "as an object in JavaScript is recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.33,
          "end": 262.65,
          "en": "And it will be a different object in memory than before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.65,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "for the last execution of the counter component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 271.26,
          "en": "and therefore it technically is a new prop value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 271.26,
          "end": 275.76,
          "en": "Now this recreation here can be prevented with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 275.76,
          "end": 279.75,
          "en": "of a special hook provided by React, which we also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 279.75,
          "end": 282.93,
          "en": "already used before in conjunction with effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 282.93,
          "end": 284.523,
          "en": "and the useEffect hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 287.403,
          "en": "It's the useCallback hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 289.38,
          "end": 294.38,
          "en": "This hook can be used to avoid the recreation of a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 295.17,
          "end": 297.15,
          "en": "and it is sometimes needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 297.15,
          "end": 301.17,
          "en": "if you have a function as a dependency of useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 301.17,
          "end": 305.13,
          "en": "And it's also needed in conjunction with memo to avoid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 307.473,
          "en": "unnecessary re‐executions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.34,
          "end": 313.34,
          "en": "Because you use useCallback by wrapping it around a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 314.67,
          "end": 316.413,
          "en": "in your component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 317.28,
          "end": 322.05,
          "en": "And then by also as a second argument by passing an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 322.05,
          "end": 324.243,
          "en": "of dependencies to useCallback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 325.08,
          "end": 329.04,
          "en": "And here you would list all props or state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 329.04,
          "end": 333.45,
          "en": "or context values you would be using inside of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 333.45,
          "end": 335.773,
          "en": "because if one of those values changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 335.773,
          "end": 338.55,
          "en": "a new function would have to be created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 338.55,
          "end": 341.763,
          "en": "so that the latest value is used in that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 342.69,
          "end": 344.94,
          "en": "But here I'm only using setCounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 344.94,
          "end": 346.92,
          "en": "which is a state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 346.92,
          "end": 350.43,
          "en": "And those state updating functions are guaranteed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 350.43,
          "end": 353.76,
          "en": "to never change by React, and therefore you don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 356.433,
          "en": "need to add them to this dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 357.99,
          "end": 362.31,
          "en": "Then useCallback returns a value in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 362.31,
          "end": 367.31,
          "en": "the same function, but in this unchanging way, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 367.77,
          "end": 371.64,
          "en": "And you can store this in a variable or constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 371.64,
          "end": 376.14,
          "en": "which I am doing here, using that same name as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 376.14,
          "end": 379.62,
          "en": "And therefore you can still use these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 379.62,
          "end": 382.106,
          "en": "as functions because they are functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 382.106,
          "end": 384.9,
          "en": "but they will be functions that are managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 384.9,
          "end": 388.653,
          "en": "by React that will not be recreated unnecessarily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 389.85,
          "end": 391.89,
          "en": "So therefore, here for handleIncrement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 391.89,
          "end": 394.56,
          "en": "I'll of course also wrap this with useCallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 394.56,
          "end": 397.053,
          "en": "and also set this dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 398.15999999999997,
          "end": 402.69,
          "en": "And with that done, if we now save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 402.69,
          "end": 406.38,
          "en": "and we reload and clear this, you'll see that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 406.38,
          "end": 410.82,
          "en": "clicking increment does not cause those icon buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 410.82,
          "end": 414.69,
          "en": "and the nested icon components to be executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 414.69,
          "end": 417.51,
          "en": "instead now it's just the counter output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 417.51,
          "end": 420.81,
          "en": "which makes sense because this, as mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 420.81,
          "end": 423.513,
          "en": "did change and does need to update.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}